mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Common Thread — Backend API\n\n## Personal puzzle generation\n\n`generatePersonalPuzzle(brief)` is an anonymous update endpoint that calls Caffeine Inference using platform-provisioned credentials. The request contains purpose (fun or study), shared interests (up to 240 characters), topic (up to 120), notes (up to 1200), difficulty (easy, balanced, or tricky), and familiarity (new or familiar). Nicknames and invitation notes are not part of the request. At least interests or topic must be nonempty.\n\nThe result is AI-produced JSON text for a proposed four-group puzzle, not trusted or fact-verified content. The frontend checks the format, field lengths, group sizes, and unique words before accepting a draft. Creators review factual accuracy and ambiguous connections before sharing. A model may instead return an error asking for more source material.\n\n## Capacity and failure\n\nA transient app-wide cooldown permits one generation start per 20 seconds, including anonymous callers; this is an initial shared capacity limit, not a per-user quota. Inference consumes the app platform budget. Output is capped at 2400 tokens and 16000 characters. Calls can take seconds and may reject on capacity, invalid input, inference, or platform credential failures. Surface failures and offer an explicit retry; never substitute an example as if it were generated. Retrying may incur another inference call.\n\n## Sharing and storage\n\nThe app does not persist generated puzzles or friend results in this canister. Casual challenge links carry a validated puzzle in their URL fragment, including its intended answers. They are not ranked or cheat-resistant. Friends' progress is independent on each screen. Study notes are not included in challenge links.\n\n## Other endpoints\n\nThe existing authorization mixin manages caller roles; generation does not require a role. OQL is registered with an empty entity list, so there are no domain tables to query. No AI credentials are returned by any app endpoint."
  };
};
